# Fixed-width subtype scaling rejects multiplication overflow

Verifies converting `127cm` to `int8<mm>` does not wrap the intermediate `1270`
magnitude before the fixed-width store boundary. The scaled magnitude is folded
while compiling, so the overflowing literal is rejected there rather than when
the value crosses into storage.

>>> source
let sizes: int8<mm>[] = [127cm]

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: array element `int8[cm]` cannot be represented as `int8[mm]` at Span { start: 25, end: 30 }

<<< exit
1
